    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW21Kuiea8rujDkU6osZp9azM)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- **Base: `443-devonthink-tags-litnote-keywords` (#443).** Merge #443 first; GitHub retargets this PR to `main` when #443 merges and its branch is deleted. Until then the diff shows only this PR's changes.\n- Reuses #443's `sp-devonthink-write-keywords`, `sp-devonthink-keywords-key` and `sp-devonthink-record-tags` (no duplicate code).\n- If merged out of order (into `main` before #443): impossible, those functions do not exist on `main`.\n- #454 (`sp-fetch-inbox`, based on `main`) also edits `sp-devonthink-browse.el` (`sp-devonthink-record-note`) and `sp-litnotes-meta.el` (`--after-create`). Different functions from this PR's (`record-tag`, `fill`); a textual conflict is possible in tests and README only.\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Request:** tags added in `sp-devonthink-browse` → `embark-act` → `sp-devonthink-record-tag` are recorded in the litnote (also when it is generated later) and mirrored into the matching BibTeX record.\n- **After tagging in the browser** (`sp-devonthink-mirror-record-tags`):\n  - Litnote: found by the record's citekey (record name without `.pdf`), `keywords` line rewritten from the record's full tags (same format as #443) and saved. A litnote open with unsaved changes is skipped and named.\n  - BibTeX: the *added* tags go into the entry's `keywords` field, after one `y-or-n-p` listing the entries. Existing keywords are kept, repeats ignored (case), `;` or `,` separator kept, field created if missing. A `.bib` buffer with unsaved changes is skipped and named.\n  - Inbox records (name not a citekey: no litnote, no entry) are skipped; the browser says how many, never an error. A failure of the mirror is reported but the tags stay in DEVONthink.\n- **Litnote generated later:** new hook `sp-litnotes-meta-fill-functions`; `sp-devonthink--fill-keywords` fills an empty `keywords` line from the record's tags. Skipped in batch fill, off macOS, for a crossref parent's record, and when the line already has a value.\n- **Options:** `sp-devonthink-bibtex-keywords` (nil = no BibTeX part), `sp-devonthink-keywords-on-fill` (nil = no fill-time tags), `sp-devonthink-keywords-key` (#443; nil = no litnote part).\n- **Not mirrored:** removals (this action only adds); tags set in DEVONthink directly.\n- Docs (bullet lists): new section \"Mirroring browser tags in litnote and BibTeX\" in `sp-devonthink-tags.org`; bullets in `sp-devonthink-browse.org` and `sp-litnotes-meta.org`; README row; `.el` re-tangled.\n- Tests (Emacs 29.3): 27 in `sp-devonthink-tags-test.el` (8 new), 9 in `sp-devonthink-browse-test.el`, 68 in `sp-litnotes-meta-test.el`, all pass. `when-let*` style only. No CHANGELOG edit.\n- **Not run** against DEVONthink, the real vault or the real `.bib` files (tests use temp files and stubs). The fill-time lookup can rebuild the record index once per new note without a record.\n\n## Manual testing\n\nMac, DEVONthink open on `literature`, a record named like a citekey with a litnote and a BibTeX entry; throw-away tag `test-tag-2`. Back up the `.bib` first (or have it under git).\n\n- [ ] Check out: `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 455-devonthink-tags-bibtex-mirror; git checkout 455-devonthink-tags-bibtex-mirror`, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`)\n- [ ] Unit tests: `cd ~/.config/emacs-modular; emacs -Q --batch -L libraries/modules/academic -L libraries/modules/funct -L libraries/modules/vulpea -l ert -l tests/sp-devonthink-tags-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit` → 27 pass (more `-L` if Emacs asks)\n- [ ] `C-c k d b`, `embark-act` on the record, `t`, tag `test-tag-2` → \"Added tags to 1 of 1 records\", then a question \"Add test-tag-2 to the BibTeX keywords of KEY?\"\n- [ ] Answer `y`: the `.bib` entry has `test-tag-2` in `keywords` (existing keywords kept), file saved\n- [ ] The litnote's `- keywords ::` line lists the record's tags and the file is saved\n- [ ] Repeat with the same tag: no duplicate in `keywords` of either file\n- [ ] Answer `n` to the question: `.bib` unchanged, litnote still updated\n- [ ] An entry without a `keywords` field: the field appears as the last one, entry still valid\n- [ ] Several marked records, one of them an inbox record (not a citekey): the others are mirrored, message \"1 record without a litnote or BibTeX entry skipped\", no `No BibTeX entry` error\n- [ ] Litnote open with unsaved edits: message names it as skipped\n- [ ] Delete the litnote of a record, tag the record, then generate the litnote (`C-c w b c` / citar): the new note has the record's tags in `keywords`\n- [ ] `(setq sp-devonthink-bibtex-keywords nil)` → no question, `.bib` untouched\n- [ ] Regression: `C-c k d t` and `C-c k d T` (#443) behave as before; `M-x sp-litnotes-meta-fill-all-dryrun` shows no DEVONthink activity\n- [ ] Clean up: remove `test-tag-2` in DEVONthink, in the `.bib` and in the litnote (`git restore`)\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard local edits: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .` (`git clean -fd` only after checking `git clean -nd`).\n- Back to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`; restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`).\n- `.bib` and litnotes: `git restore` them, or delete the `test-tag-2` entries by hand.\n- DEVONthink: remove `test-tag-2` from the tag list.\n- Fish shell works for all of the above; no yadm steps.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9b5C1yg4pV8jsNW7A)_",
